<title>UK: Heseltine talks to BA on US tie-up - paper.</title>
<headline>Heseltine talks to BA on US tie-up - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The chief of British Airways Plc, Bob Ayling, has held secret talks this week with Michael Heseltine, the deputy prime minister, to try and speed up clearance of its transatlantic tie-up with American Airlines, said the Independent on Friday.</p>
<p>Ayling is concerned that the looming UK election, due by May 22, may scupper the deal. BA managers believe that the earliest the merger could be cleared is by the summer.</p>
<p>The UK carrier has also contacted officials in the opposition Labour Party, which is riding high in opinion polls.</p>
<p>--London newdroom +44 171 5427717</p>
